# The local mock lane's bot settings that are NOT secrets — committed, so a local run needs no Railway access
# (bd-z3ze4.5). Composed into the run's .env by bot/scripts/e2e/local-stack.sh on the local lane (the default).
#
# - *_FLOW_ID: which WhatsApp Flow each feature opens. Plain ids; the mock lane plays the stored copy in
#   .claude/qa/fixtures/flows/, so these must match those fixtures (they are the staging ids).
# - WHATSAPP_TOKEN / WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN / WABA_ID / OPENROUTER_API_KEY are PLACEHOLDERS on purpose: no real
#   token and no vendor key exists in the lane, which is what keeps it from calling Meta or a paid vendor.
# - NO database or storage credential belongs here: the run's local DB and file store supply their own.

ASSESSMENT_GEN_FLOW_ID=1789313642053401
ASSESSMENT_REVIEW_FLOW_ID=1097999235912123
